\ The Hobbit (Melbourne House, 1982), from the ZX Spectrum tape.
\
\   ./telic examples/hobbit.telic [path to the .tzx]
\
\ The game's own data - the dictionary, the messages, the rooms, the
\ objects, the characters' behaviour programs, the timers and the vector
\ pictures - is read from the tape at startup (by default "The Hobbit
\ (Sinclair).tzx" in the current directory) into a 64K memory image at the
\ original addresses; the program that runs it is rewritten in telic, one
\ word for each routine of the annotated disassembly (basf-c60/thehobbitv1.0),
\ its address in the word's comment. Gandalf, Thorin, the trolls, the
\ goblins, Gollum, the dragon and the rest act on their own each turn.
\
\ Type commands as on the tape: TAKE THE SWORD, OPEN THE DOOR, SAY TO THORIN
\ "GO EAST", N, E, LOOK, INVENTORY, HELP, SCORE, SAVE, LOAD, QUIT. GRAMMAR
\ shows every action pattern and every dictionary word by class. The arrows
\ on an empty line move north, south, west and east; @ repeats the last line;
\ escape leaves. The pictures are the tape's own drawn afresh; the sound is
\ new.
\
\ The memory, the text, the parser and the execution are in
\ examples/hobbit/memory.telic ... execute.telic; the actions, the
\ characters and the special events in actions.telic, characters.telic and
\ specials.telic; the start and main loop in game.telic; the pictures in
\ pictures.telic; the window and the sound in screen.telic.

"hobbit/memory.telic" load
"hobbit/text.telic" load
"hobbit/parser.telic" load
"hobbit/utilities.telic" load
"hobbit/execute.telic" load
"hobbit/actions.telic" load
"hobbit/characters.telic" load
"hobbit/specials.telic" load
"hobbit/game.telic" load
"hobbit/pictures.telic" load
"hobbit/new-pictures.telic" load
"hobbit/screen.telic" load

\ the tape's path: the first argument, else the tape in the current directory
: tape-path ( -- path )
	args to arguments
	arguments size 0 > if arguments 0 @i exit then
	"data/hobbit.tzx" ;

\ run the game until escape or QUIT
: play ( -- )
	tape-path to path
	path file-exists? 0= if path "no tape at {0}" format . cr exit then
	path new-game
	follow-bilbo
	audio-on
	settle-effects
	screen now :idle-since ! drop
	begin screen :running @ while ' frame screen-frame repeat
	silence-audio
	audio-off ;

play
